---
interface Props{kind:'pipeline'|'targets'|'generation'}
const {kind}=Astro.props;
const labels={pipeline:['Tokenization chooses pieces; the model learns representations','Figure 1. A tokenizer maps text to vocabulary IDs. An embedding lookup gives each ID a learned vector. Context-processing layers combine those vectors; an output head produces one logit per candidate token. Token IDs themselves are not semantic coordinates.'],targets:['Shift the targets by one position','Figure 2. Each input prefix predicts the next observed token. The beginning marker supplies the first context; the end marker is a prediction target. A causal model cannot use future targets to predict an earlier position.'],generation:['Generation repeatedly feeds back the chosen token','Figure 3. A model produces a next-token distribution, a decoding policy chooses one token, and the new token extends the prefix. Repeat until an end token or a length limit. Choosing a likely token does not check whether a claim is true.']};const id='language-'+kind;
---
<figure class="diagram"><div class="figure-title"><span class="figure-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>{labels[kind][0]}</div><div class="diagram-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={labels[kind][0]}><svg viewBox="0 0 760 252" role="img" aria-labelledby={id+'-title '+id+'-desc'}><title id={id+'-title'}>{labels[kind][0]}</title><desc id={id+'-desc'}>{labels[kind][1]}</desc><defs><marker id={id+'-arrow'} markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L7 3.5 L0 7 Z" fill="var(--accent)"/></marker></defs>
{kind==='pipeline'&&<>
 {[['Text → IDs','Tokenizer vocabulary','Discrete entry numbers'],['IDs → vectors','Embedding lookup','Learned numeric features'],['Use the prefix','Context-processing layers','Order and dependencies'],['Scores → probabilities','Output head + softmax','One score per candidate']].map(([a,b,c],i)=><g><rect x={10+191*i} y="45" width="166" height="133" rx="7" class={i===1?'node node-accent':'node'}/><text x={93+191*i} y="78" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">{a}</text><text x={93+191*i} y="116" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{b}</text><text x={93+191*i} y="145" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{c}</text></g>)}
 {[0,1,2].map(i=><path d={`M${178+191*i} 110h20`} stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end={'url(#'+id+'-arrow)'}/>)}
 <text x="380" y="218" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">The tokenizer and the model must agree on the vocabulary and IDs.</text><text x="380" y="242" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">This is a neural language-model pipeline. The workbench's bigram estimates probabilities from counts.</text>
</>}
{kind==='targets'&&<>
 <text x="12" y="77" class="node-title">Input</text><text x="12" y="170" class="node-title">Target</text>
 {['<bos>','this','movie','is','fun','.'].map((word,i)=><g><rect x={91+109*i} y="43" width="98" height="52" rx="6" class="node"/><text x={140+109*i} y="75" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">{word}</text><path d={`M${140+109*i} 100v30`} stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end={'url(#'+id+'-arrow)'}/><rect x={91+109*i} y="141" width="98" height="52" rx="6" class="node node-accent"/><text x={140+109*i} y="173" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">{['this','movie','is','fun','.','<eos>'][i]}</text></g>)}
 <text x="380" y="233" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">Six scored targets. No padding in this example. The tiny bigram uses only the immediately previous token.</text>
</>}
{kind==='generation'&&<>
 {[['Current prefix','this movie is'],['Model distribution','p(next token | prefix)'],['Selection policy','greedy or sampling'],['Append token','this movie is fun']].map(([a,b],i)=><g><rect x={10+191*i} y="37" width="166" height="92" rx="7" class={i===2?'node node-accent':'node'}/><text x={93+191*i} y="70" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">{a}</text><text x={93+191*i} y="106" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">{b}</text></g>)}
 {[0,1,2].map(i=><path d={`M${178+191*i} 85h20`} stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end={'url(#'+id+'-arrow)'}/>)}
 <path d="M666 138v39H94v-40" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" marker-end={'url(#'+id+'-arrow)'}/><text x="380" y="209" text-anchor="middle" class="node-title">Repeat with the extended prefix</text><text x="380" y="241" text-anchor="middle" class="node-detail">During generation the model sees its own earlier choices; training uses observed target prefixes.</text>
</>}
</svg></div><figcaption>{labels[kind][1]}</figcaption></figure>
